;;; world/regions/hollow.map - The Hollow's rooms, laid out, with one intent
;;; each (harkfell-design section 8), approved by David on
;;; topics/harkfell-a4-region-maps ("Looks good as a start!"). Laid out
;;; seven wide and two high (x 1..7, y 2..3) rather than the sketch's 6x3:
;;; the sketch left four empty slots inside the bounds, and the rooms beside
;;; them would have had to be closed toward them (rock lids over the Rim and
;;; Scree End). Every room and intent is the sketch's.
;;;
;;;   x1   x2   x3   x4   x5   x6   x7
;;;   M -  S -  T -  B -  W -  K -  U      y2  the tops (sky above)
;;;        |    |    |    |    |    |
;;;   E -  O -  L -  H -  P -  C -  R      y3  the valley; R opens east
;;;                                            to Reedfen's Fen Edge
;;;
;;; The valley runs west to east from Scree End to the Rim and on into the
;;; fen. Three ways lead up to the tops: the Old Cut's rough face (to the
;;; Heather Shelf), the West Slope's (to the Tops) and the Chimney (to the
;;; Cairn). Every other way down is a drop: from the tops' path into the
;;; bowl, onto the Standing Stones through the Wind Gap's notch, off the
;;; Updraft Edge onto the Rim. Moth Hollow is behind the Heather Shelf's
;;; false wall. The start, the Hollow (H), has the bowl's H2 stone and,
;;; behind it, the H3 stone that seals the way down.
;;;
;;; Breaths: M, S, B, K, T (five of fourteen).
(map
  region: hollow
  origin: (1 2)
  layout:
  ("M-S-T-B-W-K-U"
   "  | | | | | |"
   "E-O-L-H-P-C-R")
  rooms:
  ((H "The Hollow" "where you wake: a bowl of turf over a low hum, and a mute stone at its heart")
   (P "Standing Stones" "a row of old standing stones to climb along, on the path between the bowl and the rim")
   (R "The Rim" "the bowl's lip, where the land drops away and the fen's sky opens below")
   (L "West Slope" "rough rock taught where a fall only lands you back in the grass")
   (O "The Old Cut" "a doorway the old people cut into the fell, blocked by fallen rock, and the wind sounding a note inside: the way to the Pipes, heard and not yet")
   (E "Scree End" "the Hollow's west edge, where scree falls into mist and birches stand far off: the way to Glasswood, not yet")
   (S "Heather Shelf" "a breath on a high shelf of heather, where reedlings feed")
   (C "The Chimney" "two walls a jump apart over soft turf: the first wall-jump, where a slip costs nothing")
   (B "Above the Bowl" "the bowl's north rim, where the stones below make a ring you can only see from here")
   (W "Wind Gap" "a notch in the fell where the wind is loudest, crossed at a run; miss, and you drop to the stones")
   (M "Moth Hollow" "a hollow behind a false wall that a careful eye finds, where the moths sleep")
   (K "Cairn" "the highest stone, alone on the top where the chimney comes out: a place to stand still")
   (T "The Tops" "the roof of the fell under the whole sky, with the fen shining far off to the east")
   (U "Updraft Edge" "seeds rising past the fell's edge higher than any jump: the way to Cloudstair, shown and not yet"))
  borders: ((R east)))
